<%# Smooth-load convention — the next page materializes behind the current one,
    then presents itself. Turbo 8 sees the view-transition meta and wraps its
    body swap in document.startViewTransition; browsers without support get
    today's instant swap. no-preview stops application visits from painting a
    stale cache snapshot before the fresh response — the current page holds
    until the new one is ready, so navigation renders exactly once. Restoration
    visits (back/forward) still restore instantly from cache. Transition
    styling: app/assets/tailwind/application.css, "Smooth-load convention". %>
<meta name="view-transition" content="same-origin">
<meta name="turbo-cache-control" content="no-preview">
